DECISIONS 263, 150, EVALUATION.md §12.2: the fold of a bound in a spends the last step while it evaluates a constant of b, so E4401 lands in b's bag and a's owner of the bound gets E3015 budget; the second bound, folded after the counter is spent, fails without a finding and gets E3015 budget too.
-- budget --
3
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

import b

/// A thing sold.
record Item {
  /// Its price.
  price: Int(0..=b.LIMIT)
  /// Its stock.
  stock: Int(0..=9)
}
-- b/b.canon --
/// B.
package b

/// The base price.
const BASE = 100

/// The highest price.
const LIMIT = BASE + 1 + 1 + 1
-- findings.txt --
error[E3015]  a/a.canon:9:18
  this refinement bound could not be folded: the evaluation budget is exhausted

error[E3015]  a/a.canon:11:14
  this refinement bound could not be folded: the evaluation budget is exhausted

error[E3015]  a/a.canon:11:18
  this refinement bound could not be folded: the evaluation budget is exhausted

error[E4401]  b/b.canon:8:15
  LIMIT: evaluation budget of 3 steps exhausted
  heaviest: a.Item (2 steps)

4 errors, 0 warnings in 2 packages (…)
